{
  "rules": [
    "Persistent low bias: model systematically underestimates realized prices, especially during uptrends. Apply an upward level shift (additive bias correction) that increases with bullish momentum.",
    "Trend/lag error: model reacts too slowly to regime changes; it forecasts sideways/mean-reverting paths while the market trends higher. Add a trend-following component (e.g., extrapolate recent 5–10d slope) rather than reverting to the 30d mean.",
    "Horizon-dependent underestimation: errors grow with forecast horizon (small early, large after ~10–15 days). Use a horizon-scaled uplift (e.g., increasing adjustment with lead time).",
    "Volatility compression: model forecasts have too small amplitude vs outcomes (misses rallies and higher highs). Inflate deviations from the starting level by a factor (>1) when recent realized volatility is rising.",
    "Breakout miss after dips: when history shows a drawdown then stabilization, the model continues to anchor low, but outcomes rebound strongly. If last price is below the 30d average and short-term momentum turns positive, override mean reversion and bias forecasts upward."
  ]
}
